aggregrate function perform a calculation on multiple rows and return a single result

example : 

Employee	Salary
Rahul	50000
Priya	60000
Amit	70000

If you want:

Total salary → SUM()
Average salary → AVG()
Highest salary → MAX()
Lowest salary → MIN()
Total employees → COUNT()

You use aggregate functions

-------------------------
GROUP BY is used to group rows having the same value in one or more columns.

It is usually used with aggregate functions:

COUNT()
SUM()
AVG()
MIN()
MAX()